{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas","id":1457930,"title":"Paradigm Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-28T17:48:46-07:00","id":1457930,"title":"Paradigm Ideas","content":"Hello. I am new here. So nice to meet you all. I have an idea for a Paradigm but give all threads on Paradigm are old. So here this is. If others want to talk about there own ideas first please do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27030-gale1","name":"Gale1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T15:31:28-07:00","id":1459776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gale1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas#post1457930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I am new here. So nice to meet you all. I have an idea for a Paradigm but give all threads on Paradigm are old. So here this is. If others want to talk about there own ideas first please do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like Utopian Etherites. Make the world better. Are you a player or storyteller?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T17:03:59-07:00","id":1459792,"title":"","content":"General forum suggestion: if you start the thread, then start the conversation. Seed ideas to harvest discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T08:52:16-07:00","id":1459851,"title":"","content":"Paradigm has changed a bit in meaning over the years, so it isn't 100% clear what we are talking about here. Do you mean a particular magical practice (invokes the true names of the angels, exploits nth dimensional physical principles, hacks the base code of reality, etc.)? Or do you mean magical philosophies (the world is fundamentally mechanistic, the world is fundamentally alive and adaptive, it's all an illusion, etc.)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T17:45:34-07:00","id":1460767,"title":"","content":"@HorzionParty2021, Mainly Player. But also someone who is reading the lore a lot and kind is trapped just reading the setting. @monteparans Sorry, I am new and well. Was not sure if anyone wanted to hear the idea. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Both I guess? Becaues there both a part of the same thing yet sperate at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27030-gale1","user":"Gale1","date":". 09-21-2021, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27030-gale1","name":"Gale1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T10:30:46-07:00","id":1461238,"title":"","content":"Two important questions to begin with regarding Paradigm, in my opinion: What is Magic? And where does it come from? Sometimes those two combine into one question.<br /> <br /> An important thing to consider is whether or not, from the perspective of the Paradigm (regardless of actual mechanics about the Avatar, etc.), Magic is Internal or External, or the extent that it is either. Does the power come from within the Mage, or is it the power of spirits, gods, etc., that the Mage is granted, wields, controls through science, etc.? Is it some combination, with an Internal component required to use the External power?<br /> <br /> I tend to lean towards chaos magic myself these days, an individualistic and pragmatic approach fit for a wishy-washy skeptic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T15:35:14-07:00","id":1461429,"title":"","content":"Ok that reminds me of my idea. Which is a Internal? I think, its a werid one. The core idea is Humanity has a collective unconsciousness. It sees thing mainly via a Psionics, as in everyone could do this if they go through certain things. But in that collective unconsciousness ideas exist and have power. The Psion has power over the unconsciousness and can use there mind to effect the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27030-gale1","name":"Gale1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:31:32-07:00","id":1461444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gale1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1461429#post1461429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok that reminds me of my idea. Which is a Internal? I think, its a werid one. The core idea is Humanity has a collective unconsciousness. It sees thing mainly via a Psionics, as in everyone could do this if they go through certain things. But in that collective unconsciousness ideas exist and have power. The Psion has power over the unconsciousness and can use there mind to effect the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>What tradition/Convention is your character? What kind of Sphere build suits the Paradigm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T22:58:14-07:00","id":1461484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gale1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1461429#post1461429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok that reminds me of my idea. Which is a Internal? I think, its a werid one. The core idea is Humanity has a collective unconsciousness. It sees thing mainly via a Psionics, as in everyone could do this if they go through certain things. But in that collective unconsciousness ideas exist and have power. The Psion has power over the unconsciousness and can use there mind to effect the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like a blend between External, the majority of the Collective Unconscious being made up of other minds, but also Internal, to the extent that your mind is part of the Collective Unconscious. My personal Chaos Magic Paradigm also sees the mind as a significant component of Magic.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert, but Psionics are most often associated with more scientific Paradigms IIRC. They're rare among the Technocracy, and heavily monitored. I could definitely see a psychic theorist among the Etherites as well. Don't know as much about the Virtual Adepts, but I don't know if it meshes as well with their perspective.<br /> <br /> Depending on what Edition you're looking at, you're going to need to consider that you will often be required, by game rules, to use Instruments other than pure thought. Or if you really want to go that route, considering ways to balance it against other characters with a less flexible Paradigm.<br /> <br /> P.S. It's actually not a super weird Paradigm, and I can even probably think of a way to describe it in the terms of Mage mechanics. Mage already includes the concept of the Consensus, that what is possible, impossible, and supernatural is at least significantly influenced by the collective beliefs of humanity. Your Paradigm could possibly be described as the idea that the Consensus is the Collective Unconsciousness that the Psion manipulates, and Magic is essentially the consequence of temporary alterations of the local Consensus aimed towards a particular result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 09-26-2021, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T04:15:58-07:00","id":1461542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gale1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1461429#post1461429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok that reminds me of my idea. Which is a Internal? I think, its a werid one. The core idea is Humanity has a collective unconsciousness. It sees thing mainly via a Psionics, as in everyone could do this if they go through certain things. But in that collective unconsciousness ideas exist and have power. The Psion has power over the unconsciousness and can use there mind to effect the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s very workable, and possibly all you need. <br /> <br /> Two additional considerations:<br /> <br /> 1) What skills does your character use to do these? Though not every ST brings it up, characters usually need certain training and skill. Psychology and mediation for instance.<br /> <br /> 2) Are there any common effects or spheres that you can\u2019t think of this paradigm using. If so, you might want to briefly consider what research someone of the paradigm might do if the wanted to expand their capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T06:10:50-07:00","id":1461549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1461444#post1461444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What tradition/Convention is your character? What kind of Sphere build suits the Paradigm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking either Hollow one or a werid person in the Chorus. I don't think Son of Ether would work give, they wouldn't see Ether. <br /> <br /> @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\">Ramnesis</a> </b> I am thinking most likely HR, or other normalish things. At lest for a part of it. But I thinking it would be a psychologists who might of meet some Numinist users who are psychics for at lest backstory and skills. As for spheres? I am thinking Mind. Spirit, and Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <b>@<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\">Kharnov</a></b> As for how to cast, like I said most likely normaish thing but I can also see maybe some eye contact for some of the things, while tech mainly becaues human made tools would work best for the Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27030-gale1","name":"Gale1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T08:51:19-07:00","id":1461557,"title":"","content":"Yep, subtler and more &quot;normal&quot; choices for Instruments are fine, just need to make sure you determine what Effects can be performed using what Instruments.<br /> <br /> It does seem like a bit of an odd fit for the Chorus, but I could see it working. You would probably need to add some kind of religious aspect or element to your character's belief system, even if it's not a big part of how they actually practice Magic. Hollow Ones are one of my favourite Crafts, but they're pretty much the opposite end of the Chorus, I think. I could be wrong about this, but I think that the Etherites do take in people who ascribe to other &quot;scientific&quot; theories than Luminiferous Ether.<br /> <br /> How does Spirit/the Umbra fit into your character concept? Does your character view it as the realm of the Collective Unconscious, are they different things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T10:48:55-07:00","id":1461572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1461557#post1461557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, subtler and more &quot;normal&quot; choices for Instruments are fine, just need to make sure you determine what Effects can be performed using what Instruments.<br /> <br /> It does seem like a bit of an odd fit for the Chorus, but I could see it working. You would probably need to add some kind of religious aspect or element to your character's belief system, even if it's not a big part of how they actually practice Magic. Hollow Ones are one of my favourite Crafts, but they're pretty much the opposite end of the Chorus, I think. I could be wrong about this, but I think that the Etherites do take in people who ascribe to other &quot;scientific&quot; theories than Luminiferous Ether.<br /> <br /> How does Spirit/the Umbra fit into your character concept? Does your character view it as the realm of the Collective Unconscious, are they different things?</div> </div> </div> </div>OK yeah that is fair on the Chorus bits. I would also think a Orphan could work for it if they don't get found by Ether or Crats. Umbra is the Collective Unconscious, but thanks to that it holds a lot of things that are mad. Because its not just facts, beliefs, its also daydreams and nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27030-gale1","name":"Gale1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T08:47:09-07:00","id":1461962,"title":"","content":"My last two characters were both Etherites, but each with a little spin.<br /> <br /> The first was a ghost hunter. He ran with a crew of sleepers on ghost hunting trips, exploring abandoned buildings, uploading videos to youtube, etc. He designed, or at least modified, all of their equipment, and was generally the man behind the camera. Some of his devices were pretty normal- specially designed microphones, cameras, night vision goggles, etc which he modified to tap into &quot;etheric frequencies.&quot; He also borrowed a lot from the trappings of spiritualism and mediumship and the like, and tried to create devices to emulate these practices. For instance, instead of holding a proper seance, he might surround a crystal ball with etheric resonators to replicate what (he thinks) is going on when a seance is held. Or he might hook a spirit board up to a machine with a keyboard and printer... to help facilitate communication, you understand.<br /> <br /> The second was for a one-shot set in Berlin shortly before the fall of the wall. He was a psychologist who also helped people cross over with his credentials as a practicing psychiatrist as well as his talent for hypnosis. This Etherite was much less focused on gadgetry and more about connecting his consciousness with the ether. He created custom drugs, used meditation, psychotherapy, psychoanalysis, etc. He believed he could harmonize his mind with others by getting them to think the same thing he was thinking at the same time, creating &quot;etheric synchronicity&quot; allowing him to communicate telepathically. He would do this by showing his allies Zener cards and trying to guess what card they were seeing. He didn't announce his guess or anything, in fact, he usually just assumed he was right and put the card back in the deck. But one of my favorite effects he tried (and failed) was a scenario where they were meeting someone and he wanted to read his mind on the sly. He couldn't use his usual instruments for mind reading (electrodes placed on the forehead, or synchronicity) so he got creative. They were enjoying cigars and bourbon, so he dropped one of his pills into his own drink, dipped the cigar in the bourbon (like you do) and blew a puff of smoke at his host. Unfortunately the effect failed and worse, he recognized the Effect for what it was, and got sent packing.<br /> <br /> I should mention both characters at one time or another made use of a colander placed on the head connected with wires and blinking lights to &quot;enhance&quot; their psychic powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:51:43-07:00","id":1462045,"title":"","content":"Players and STs face conflicting requirements:<br /> <br /> - If the player tries to fit their paradigm to the rules that they are learning, they face being accused of using the Purple Paradigm and not truly roleplaying Mage.<br /> <br /> - If they player puts a lot of work into coming up with an original Paradigm, they may be disappointed when the storyteller says that the rules prevent them from doing something that their Paradigm says that their ranks in Spheres should allow them to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T04:41:49-07:00","id":1462118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462045#post1462045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players and STs face conflicting requirements:<br /> <br /> - If they player puts a lot of work into coming up with an original Paradigm, they may be disappointed when the storyteller says that the rules prevent them from doing something that their Paradigm says that their ranks in Spheres should allow them to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I originally read this as issues when a character's Paradigm won't allow an effect that the Spheres would, which is something the player and the ST should work together to overcome. I can't think of a situation where a character's Paradigm would even be expected to upgrade the way the Spheres - the game mechanics Spheres - work. The closest thing I can think of is specialty spheres but the player knows when they are using those.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-30-2021, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:34:14-07:00","id":1462221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462118#post1462118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I originally read this as issues when a character's Paradigm won't allow an effect that the Spheres would, which is something the player and the ST should work together to overcome. I can't think of a situation where a character's Paradigm would even be expected to upgrade the way the Spheres - the game mechanics Spheres - work. The closest thing I can think of is specialty spheres but the player knows when they are using those.</div> </div> </div> </div>The player comes up with a character concept where his character has been reincarnated. His previous incarnation was a legendary Mystic Mage. He fully recalls the world as it was before guns were introduced to the Consensus. He sees the modern world as an illusion. He takes Time 3 and Forces 3. The player says that, with those two Spheres, he should be able to draw from the previous incarnation's true understanding of reality before the illusion was perpetrated on the world to be immune to bullets and not incur Paradox for being seen by sleepers to resist machine-gun fire. It's an original Paradigm. Why should the player not be able to do this if they have put careful thought into this concept? And, if the effort to create an original Paradigm doesn't merit some bending of the rules, why is Purple Paradigm a pejorative term? It's like, &quot;Be original... Oh, you can't do that because rules... Oh, you just want to conform to the rules so you can get on with playing? - PURPLE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:59:19-07:00","id":1462225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462221#post1462221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player comes up with a character concept where his character has been reincarnated. His previous incarnation was a legendary Mystic Mage. He fully recalls the world as it was before guns were introduced to the Consensus. He sees the modern world as an illusion. He takes Time 3 and Forces 3. The player says that, with those two Spheres, he should be able to draw from the previous incarnation's true understanding of reality before the illusion was perpetrated on the world to be immune to bullets and not incur Paradox for being seen by sleepers to resist machine-gun fire. It's an original Paradigm. Why should the player not be able to do this if they have put careful thought into this concept? And, if the effort to create an original Paradigm doesn't merit some bending of the rules, why is Purple Paradigm a pejorative term? It's like, &quot;Be original... Oh, you can't do that because rules... Oh, you just want to conform to the rules so you can get on with playing? - PURPLE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what Paradigm means in the game. Your Paradigm states what your magic does and how, the Consensus states if it is vulgar. No paradigm can ignore the Consensus and your Spheres still need to be enough to make your effects even if your Paradigm blurs some lines, although in this case he probably can do this effect.<br /> <br /> Consensus isn't a matter of memory, reaching to the past wouldn't make him immune to the now, much less to the current Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T03:31:00-07:00","id":1462260,"title":"","content":"There is a name for a mage with a paradigm that lets him or her define what's Vulgar and what's Coincidental. Marauder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T06:04:23-07:00","id":1462271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462221#post1462221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The player comes up with a character concept where his character has been reincarnated. His previous incarnation was a legendary Mystic Mage. He fully recalls the world as it was before guns were introduced to the Consensus. He sees the modern world as an illusion. He takes Time 3 and Forces 3. The player says that, with those two Spheres, he should be able to draw from the previous incarnation's true understanding of reality before the illusion was perpetrated on the world to be immune to bullets and not incur Paradox for being seen by sleepers to resist machine-gun fire. It's an original Paradigm. Why should the player not be able to do this if they have put careful thought into this concept? And, if the effort to create an original Paradigm doesn't merit some bending of the rules, why is Purple Paradigm a pejorative term? It's like, &quot;Be original... Oh, you can't do that because rules... Oh, you just want to conform to the rules so you can get on with playing? - PURPLE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;purple paradigm' is not a pejorative for using the game rules. It is a pejorative for treating the game rules as an actual paradigm or as an in world metaphysics rather than a gaming abstraction. It applies when people make their character have a paradigm like &quot;The world is made up of nine spheres and if I know enough about them I can make things happen&quot; and then using that to try and bypass elements like instruments or paradox. It also was a major source of contention in the Revised era because lots of people assumed that the &quot;purple paradigm&quot; was a universal thing mages started defaulting to as they gained Arete and shed instruments. M20 is a little clearer on what shedding instruments means.<br /> <br /> The example character you gave works as an original paradigm (I think. I'm presuming he's essentially using the paradigm of his past self, whatever that is). The player can do that. He still needs to have the right spheres for the effects he wants because he's still playing the same game as everyone else. He still gets hit with paradox too (when appropriate), because like many (most?) mages his paradigm does not play well with the consensus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:39:57-07:00","id":1462351,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462225#post1462225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what Paradigm means in the game. Your Paradigm states what your magic does and how, the Consensus states if it is vulgar. No paradigm can ignore the Consensus and your Spheres still need to be enough to make your effects even if your Paradigm blurs some lines, although in this case he probably can do this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This example was meant to highlight the potential for each player's obligation to invent a Paradigm to cause problems. It applies to a Tradition Chronicle, more so than a Technocracy Chronicle. The conflict is right there in what you just said: YOUR (player's) Paradigm states what Magick can do... Versus: No Paradigm can ignore the Consensus... It is a balancing act that my troupe has managed well. For one player, we watched YouTube videos of an official Pagan Association. Her character's Paradigm has elements of &quot;Power Comes From the Gods&quot;. In the context of the setting, it has &quot;Nature Must Be Defended&quot;. A lot of her spells are self-targeted and Coincidental, a few being Vulgar Without Witnesses.<br /> <br /> There is a trend in Ascension where more and more people want to play Technocracy, which I don't think is bad at all. They are opting for a game where using Techno-Magick is the default and doesn't require any mental gymnastics to create an effect. Paradigm fits Consensus. Also, I am not talking about Hyper-Technology. Tradition Mages in populated cities have to act like Technocracy Mages in terms of the effects they are creating in order to avoid Paradox.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462225#post1462225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consensus isn't a matter of memory, reaching to the past wouldn't make him immune to the now, much less to the current Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose that, in his current incarnation, he was raised in a mystic village in a Primal Reality Zone. People have been living there for thousands of years and live happily by the old ways, which they describe in oral tradition as well as written texts. He might choose Correspondence instead of Time. While in the city, he uses Correspondence and Forces to make an area around him operate under the physical laws that function in the Primal reality Zone, where guns don't work. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462260#post1462260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a name for a mage with a paradigm that lets him or her define what's Vulgar and what's Coincidental. Marauder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Madness beckons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462271#post1462271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;purple paradigm' is not a pejorative for using the game rules. It is a pejorative for treating the game rules as an actual paradigm or as an in world metaphysics rather than a gaming abstraction. It applies when people make their character have a paradigm like &quot;The world is made up of nine spheres and if I know enough about them I can make things happen&quot; and then using that to try and bypass elements like instruments or paradox. It also was a major source of contention in the Revised era because lots of people assumed that the &quot;purple paradigm&quot; was a universal thing mages started defaulting to as they gained Arete and shed instruments. M20 is a little clearer on what shedding instruments means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was in 1st Edition that the Verbena had to use a Cauldron as their focus for Life Magick. I made a Verbena character and neglected to take Resources as a background. This had me asking my ST if I could own a pickup truck for the purpose of transporting the cauldron. Not long after, I learned that Black Suits could use their handgun as a focus for Mind Magick, &quot;Surrender!&quot;. With me thinking that surrendering to the Technocracy might actually a better option than getting shot and having the combined increase to the difficulty on Life Magick from being wounded and not having my cauldron on hand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462271#post1462271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The example character you gave works as an original paradigm (I think. I'm presuming he's essentially using the paradigm of his past self, whatever that is). The player can do that. He still needs to have the right spheres for the effects he wants because he's still playing the same game as everyone else. He still gets hit with paradox too (when appropriate), because like many (most?) mages his paradigm does not play well with the consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;using the paradigm of his past self&quot; is what I meant, correct. It's not a character I would try to play or slip past the storyteller to get away with Consensus-breaking effects. A Paradox-ridden NPC maybe. <br /> <br /> The degree to which I enforce Paradigm and Focus requirements and how is influenced by some IRL factors that I suspect differ from most people here. I am not part of any local gaming club. The people I play with were new to both Mage and RP, generally, when I introduced the game. If I had tried to sell Mage while suggesting that you have to pass an essay-exam on Paradigm in order to begin play, it would have been a tough sell. My approach is less &quot;front end&quot; and puts more emphasis on Vision for the World.<br /> <br /> For comparison, let's say you have a character, beginning as a sleeper, who has an optimistic vision for the world. They believe that it is possible to change the world for the better in the near future. They Awaken and are recruited into the Euthanatos Tradition and learn about The Wheel of Ages. Their Mentor teaches them that they are currently in an Age Darkness, soon to be followed by an Age of Sorrows. This aspect of their Paradigm will significantly influence what they can do with Magick and how they cast. The character might have a surprisingly optimistic Vision for the World that somehow fits their Tradition (accelerate the wheel to skip the next age), an aspect of their Personal Paradigm. In standard play, the emphasis is on the current metaphysical understanding of reality, not the vision toward which they are trying to influence the world.<br /> <br /> By making Vision for the World as important as Paradigm Metaphysics, I allowed the development of each character's Paradigm to be extended over the course of the whole Chronicle, rather than compacted into an awkward essay-exam that they must pass before the end of session zero. The vision of an ideal world that the character is trying to push into the Consensus shapes the type of Magick they can do. I will be getting more into Resonance effects as the campaign rolls forward. We all started with some amount of Arcane for survivability's sake, but will be exploring the benefits of high personal Resonance in the context of Paradigm.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T18:44:32-07:00","id":1462374,"title":"","content":"First let me clarify that I see nothing wrong with your play-style or take on Paradigm. I'm just talking rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462351#post1462351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe conflict is right there in what you just said: YOUR (player's) Paradigm states what Magick can do... Versus: No Paradigm can ignore the Consensus...</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems that you mixed up a little what is the Consensus with what is your Paradigm. And maybe the focus of the misunderstanding is the Paradox.<br /> <br /> Paradox isn't anti-magic. Paradox isn't the impossibility of magic. Casting a fireball will incur Paradox, but the fireball is still cast. It is supported by the caster Paradigm, but not by the Consensus, and the Consensus punish you for breaking HIS Paradigm.<br /> <br /> So the idea of a character that brings his Paradigm from their past life is absolutely valid, but in no way that implies immunity to current Consensus, the Consensus will keep punishing them for breaking its perceived rules.<br /> <br /> No Paradigm includes the idea of Paradox, they just try to understand it. The Paradigm states that reality works in a given way (it doesn't) and magic is the Mage using the laws of this theory of reality to do stuff. But the Consensus is the Paradigm of the entire mass of humanity, and it is a vengeful Mage. It makes its own magic all the time, we just call it natural laws, but it doesn't use countermagic, instead it retaliates with Paradox. Something that is by nature absent in the original theory of the Mage, creating an unpredicted consequence.<br /> <br /> The Mage can have absolutely any explanation on their Paradigm of why they aren't prone to Paradox. They still are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462351#post1462351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in the city, he uses Correspondence and Forces to make an area around him operate under the physical laws that function in the Primal reality Zone, where guns don't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>First it would be an effect, not a Paradigm. And second, if they could really pull out that effect (which I think would be more complex than just two Spheres and would at least use Prime, not Forces), then yes, that would work precisely like that, so what? It would still not be a consequence of their Paradigm, but of a legal Effect.<br /> <br /> And just to be sure, the idea of a Paradigm using indirect explanations to sidestep the rules was already covered by talks on Spiritual Paradigms, 'cause they're this kind of situation and are actually quite common. A shaman may explain every effect as talking to the spirits to get results, but isn't excused to make everything just with Spirit. If the shaman asks the spirits to create a plastic bag out of thin air they need the same level of Matter as anyone making the same, but probably explain out their mastery of Matter as understanding the spirits of physical things. And despite spirits not being subject to Paradox, the shaman is and it is just as incomprehensible to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T18:55:53-07:00","id":1462376,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't go so far as to say that no paradigm includes paradox. Rather, the way they include Paradox it's \u201cwhat happens when things go wrong?\u201d and things will go wrong. That much is inevitable. <br /> <br /> Put another way: Paradox will happen regardless of your paradigm. But the exact form it takes depends on your Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T19:29:39-07:00","id":1462381,"title":"","content":"And what I mentioned about Marauders before: Marauders have the ability to force their paradigm onto the local reality zone. No one else does. There is no magic that can allow you to change what is coincidencal and what is vulgar. And your paradigm does not determine what is coincidental and what is vulgar; the local reality Zone does that. If a mage does a call-back to a time when the Consensus was different, he still has to contend with the <i>current</i> Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T20:03:59-07:00","id":1462385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462376#post1462376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go so far as to say that no paradigm includes paradox. Rather, the way they include Paradox it's \u201cwhat happens when things go wrong?\u201d and things will go wrong. That much is inevitable.<br /> <br /> Put another way: Paradox will happen regardless of your paradigm. But the exact form it takes depends on your Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to be didactic, but yes, your Paradigm may include Paradox, or better saying, an explanation to Paradox. And Paradox may use this explanation if it seems appropriate, something it frequently does with the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T23:41:04-07:00","id":1462405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462374#post1462374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First let me clarify that I see nothing wrong with your play-style or take on Paradigm. I'm just talking rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> It seems that you mixed up a little what is the Consensus with what is your Paradigm. And maybe the focus of the misunderstanding is the Paradox.<br /> <br /> Paradox isn't anti-magic. Paradox isn't the impossibility of magic. Casting a fireball will incur Paradox, but the fireball is still cast. It is supported by the caster Paradigm, but not by the Consensus, and the Consensus punish you for breaking HIS Paradigm.<br /> <br /> So the idea of a character that brings his Paradigm from their past life is absolutely valid, but in no way that implies immunity to current Consensus, the Consensus will keep punishing them for breaking its perceived rules.<br /> <br /> No Paradigm includes the idea of Paradox, they just try to understand it. The Paradigm states that reality works in a given way (it doesn't) and magic is the Mage using the laws of this theory of reality to do stuff. But the Consensus is the Paradigm of the entire mass of humanity, and it is a vengeful Mage. It makes its own magic all the time, we just call it natural laws, but it doesn't use countermagic, instead it retaliates with Paradox. Something that is by nature absent in the original theory of the Mage, creating an unpredicted consequence.<br /> <br /> The Mage can have absolutely any explanation on their Paradigm of why they aren't prone to Paradox. They still are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand all of this. The player whose character I described (two versions of) is a hypothetical player who makes an error in interpretation under the pressure to pump out a Paradigm on the Front End before the end of session zero. I was actually trying to say something different: Conflict between Player's Original Paradigm (POP - nice acronym) and the Rules that govern what is possible with Spheres at the level the player has them at, Regardless of Paradox. Consensus was the wrong word to use. POP vs RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462374#post1462374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First it would be an effect, not a Paradigm. And second, if they could really pull out that effect (which I think would be more complex than just two Spheres and would at least use Prime, not Forces), then yes, that would work precisely like that, so what? It would still not be a consequence of their Paradigm, but of a legal Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would Prime permit nullifying the functionality of guns? Is there something I am missing about the Sphere? My character has it at 3, so I would love to know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462374#post1462374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just to be sure, the idea of a Paradigm using indirect explanations to sidestep the rules was already covered by talks on Spiritual Paradigms, 'cause they're this kind of situation and are actually quite common. A shaman may explain every effect as talking to the spirits to get results, but isn't excused to make everything just with Spirit. If the shaman asks the spirits to create a plastic bag out of thin air they need the same level of Matter as anyone making the same, but probably explain out their mastery of Matter as understanding the spirits of physical things. And despite spirits not being subject to Paradox,</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I always saw the Dreamspeakers as potentially the most powerful Tradition due to Spirit being their Tradition-Affinity Sphere. The Avatar Storm barred access to the places where they have the greatest advantage and with which they are most familiar (for those who use this metaplot element, not me). Satyros has often spoken about regretting how the Dreamspeakers were depicted, which leaves me to wonder why, when he was the lead developer, they basically junked the Umbra as a part of the setting. Does techno-shamanism improve how Dreamspeakers are depicted, modernizing them? What advantages are there to taking Spirit over Matter for improving machines? <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T00:38:48-07:00","id":1462406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457930-paradigm-ideas?p=1462405#post1462405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Prime permit nullifying the functionality of guns?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about jamming guns, but about bringing the laws of the Reality Zone. Since Correspondence (at a high level) really can superimpose two locations, an effect could theoretically use this to actually bring the rules of a Reality Zone to somewhere else.<br /> <br /> This was just me thinking about possible effects and not thoroughly yet. And doing that would be vulgar on its own, but could still have a lot of interesting results.<br /> <br /> On the matter of the Dreamspeakers, I don't think Spirit is so much better than other Spheres. It may be incredibly versatile, but you're still doing everything indirectly and being dependent on the results the spirits can and will really get. As someone said before, it depends a lot on the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}